      "message": "feat(post): LN2W wire offset - lead-out rule, true notes for an offset program\n\nReview of PR #4139, findings 1 to 4.\n\n- wire_offset.rs: the move that cancels the offset gets the rule of the\n  move that engages it (one helper, _woLead): stated end points, a length\n  above zero, and at least the offset radius. A G40 on a move of no\n  length or a shorter one is refused by name.\n- The engine publishes programOffsets before onOpen: one entry for each\n  section, \"control\", \"wear\" or \"\". sodick-ln2w.cps writes the header and\n  the section notes from it. An offset program does not say \"NO WIRE\n  OFFSET\", and a section on the control's offset does not say that the\n  kerf is in the path. A program without a COMP record is byte-identical.\n- assets/posts/AGENTS.md, docs/CNC-INTERMEDIATE.md and the decision\n  record state the offset form, the helper, the refusals and the pins.\n- New pins in crates/post/tests/sodick_ln2w/offset.rs: the lead-out\n  refusals and a lead-out of exactly the radius, the notes of an offset\n  program, a change of side while the offset is on, and the H999 limit.\n\nThis change is a new capability (issue #4076 is an enhancement), so the\ntype is feat.\n\nRefs #4076\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
